WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:18.287
Zoe was listening to Chase Gibson's newest song while doing research for her hero project.

2
00:00:19.107 --> 00:00:26.974
Her project partner, Amanda, had already made a list of possible heroes—all politicians, artists, and scientists.

3
00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:32.431
"Boring," Zoe thought after reading about Amanda's fifth-choice pick.

4
00:00:33.091 --> 00:00:36.814
Amanda had already said no to Zoe's first choice—Chase Gibson.

5
00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:39.277
He was her favorite singer.

6
00:00:39.737 --> 00:00:41.418
And he could dance and act too.

7
00:00:41.438 --> 00:00:44.601
"But how has he changed the world?"

8
00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:46.623
Amanda had asked at school that day.

9
00:00:46.643 --> 00:00:50.066
"Besides, I read he isn't even that nice."

10
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.228
Zoe didn't care.

11
00:00:53.028 --> 00:00:57.152
Maybe she could still persuade Amanda that Chase was talented enough to write about.

12
00:00:57.952 --> 00:01:02.035
Taking a break, she pulled up the official Chase Gibson fan website.

13
00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:04.677
She could hardly believe her eyes.

14
00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:08.459
"Aaah!" Zoe's scream echoed through the house.

15
00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:10.321
"Zoe, what's wrong?

16
00:01:10.341 --> 00:01:10.941
What happened?"

17
00:01:11.642 --> 00:01:14.003
Zoe turned around to see Mom in the doorway.

18
00:01:14.023 --> 00:01:18.306
"Chase Gibson is coming to the mall this Saturday to sign autographs!"

19
00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.187
Mom frowned.

20
00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:23.990
"Never scream like that, unless you're hurt or in danger."

21
00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.531
"Can I go?

22
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:26.692
Please, Mom!"

23
00:01:27.384 --> 00:01:30.807
"You and Amanda are working on your project on Saturday," Mom said.

24
00:01:30.827 --> 00:01:33.109
"Schoolwork comes first, you know."

25
00:01:33.129 --> 00:01:35.251
"But Mom!"

26
00:01:35.652 --> 00:01:36.352
Zoe pleaded.

27
00:01:36.372 --> 00:01:39.695
"Zoe, no," Mom said firmly.

28
00:01:39.715 --> 00:01:42.017
"Now turn that music down please.

29
00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:43.859
Dinner will be ready soon."

30
00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.903
Zoe slouched down and lowered the volume as Mom headed downstairs.

31
00:01:48.924 --> 00:01:53.548
"I have to go to the mall this Saturday," she thought.

32
00:01:55.376 --> 00:01:59.857
After waiting in line for over an hour, Zoe finally stepped up to the table.

33
00:02:00.678 --> 00:02:05.659
Seeing Chase Gibson in person made her forget all about the big lie she'd told her mother.

34
00:02:05.679 --> 00:02:06.960
"Hi, Chase!

35
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.320
I'm your biggest fan!"

36
00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.860
Zoe said to the star.

37
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.061
"Can you sign some things To Zoe, without a y?"

38
00:02:13.922 --> 00:02:17.703
She emptied her backpack filled with Chase Gibson merchandise onto the table.

39
00:02:18.543 --> 00:02:21.744
Chase Gibson looked at Zoe and then at the pile of stuff.

40
00:02:23.148 --> 00:02:24.588
"I can't sign all that!"

41
00:02:24.909 --> 00:02:25.529
he snapped.

42
00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:28.369
"I've been signing autographs for hours!

43
00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.250
And look at that line!"

44
00:02:33.331 --> 00:02:34.951
Zoe felt a lump in her throat.

45
00:02:34.971 --> 00:02:38.352
"But I'm your—" "Biggest fan?

46
00:02:38.372 --> 00:02:39.272
Yes, I know.

47
00:02:39.332 --> 00:02:40.773
That's what everyone says.

48
00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:43.614
Now pick one thing, and I'll sign it.

49
00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:45.834
Let's keep this line moving."

50
00:02:46.714 --> 00:02:49.015
Zoe shyly unrolled a small poster.

51
00:02:49.815 --> 00:02:52.216
Chase Gibson quickly scribbled an autograph on it.

52
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.862
As Zoe walked away from the table, she looked at the autograph: To Zoey, —Chase Gibson it read

53
00:02:59.902 --> 00:03:01.302
in big ugly letters.

54
00:03:01.322 --> 00:03:05.744
"Ugh." Just then her phone beeped.

55
00:03:06.624 --> 00:03:08.204
It was a text message from Mom.

56
00:03:09.085 --> 00:03:10.305
Come home right now!

57
00:03:10.325 --> 00:03:14.306
"You lied about where you were going!"

58
00:03:15.126 --> 00:03:16.427
Mom's eyes narrowed.

59
00:03:16.447 --> 00:03:20.688
"I had no idea where you were when Amanda's mom called!

60
00:03:21.472 --> 00:03:24.054
Then I remembered that Chase Gibson was at the mall today."

61
00:03:24.935 --> 00:03:26.796
Zoe winced at hearing that name.

62
00:03:26.816 --> 00:03:28.517
"I'm sorry, Mom."

63
00:03:28.537 --> 00:03:31.659
"I'll talk with you about some consequences later.

64
00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.741
For now, go to your room.

65
00:03:34.061 --> 00:03:36.062
Amanda will be here soon to work on your project.

66
00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.124
I hope you've learned a lesson!"

67
00:03:38.144 --> 00:03:42.126
"Oh, I learned a big lesson today," Zoe murmured.

68
00:03:42.987 --> 00:03:44.548
Zoe trudged off to her room.

69
00:03:45.389 --> 00:03:49.772
She flung her backpack, still filled with Chase Gibson stuff, onto the floor.

70
00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.081
She reached for her notebook.

71
00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:55.724
A Chase Gibson sticker smiled at her on the cover.

72
00:03:56.605 --> 00:03:57.886
Zoe stared back at him.

73
00:03:57.906 --> 00:03:59.968
"I still like your music.

74
00:04:00.869 --> 00:04:03.491
But Amanda was right—you're not a hero."

75
00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:08.715
She flipped open the notebook and began searching for a hero from Amanda's list.
